{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": "All hex strings are lowercase. Byte-exact cross-language test vectors for the NTAG424 DNA / boltcard crypto stack. See README.md for the schema and the consumer update flow. 'counter_bytes' is the 3-byte SDMReadCtr exactly as stored in PICCData[8..11] and SV2[13..16] (SV2 copies the PICC bytes verbatim); libraries differ on whether they interpret this field as little- or big-endian, so the vectors pin the BYTES, not an integer. Optional per-vector flag \"negative\": true marks a REJECT vector: the input p/c must be refused by a conforming SDM verification chain (decrypt gate failure or SUN-MAC mismatch); consumers assert rejection instead of comparing intermediates. Vectors whose origin starts with \"cross-impl audit A2\" are reference-executed (two independent implementations run, byte-identical); \"cross-impl audit A3 transcription-derived\" vectors were generated from a line-cited transcription of the Go reference and validated against pre-existing reference vectors.",
